 Mod clones rewrite their own `mods/<name>/` asset paths and self-opening
 overlay names to the new name.
 
+**Patcher (this setup):** changes to Herdr's own behavior that settings or a
+separate mod can't reach are kept as patches by the `patcher` mod, in
+`mods/patcher/patches/`. At every start it rebuilds patched copies of Herdr's
+originals (`mods/my-*`, `layouts/my-main.json`, and this file) so they follow
+Herdr's updates. Never edit those copies; edit the patches. How it works and
+how to add or fix a patch: `mods/patcher/README.md`.
+
+**Shared status (this setup):** `mods/status-hub` fetches each space's git facts,
+worktrees and PR/MR status once and publishes them as shared `status.*` keys
+(contract: `mods/status-hub/README.md`); a new mod reads those instead of running
+git or gh itself.
+
 If you edit a shipped file anyway, the next start moves it to
 `<name>-edited` (a mod folder or layout JSON; a number is added if taken),
 copies its layout clicks, restores Herdr's version and shows a toast.
